<title>UK: Matra Marconi wins Brazil satcoms deal.</title>
<headline>Matra Marconi wins Brazil satcoms deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matra Marconi Space said on Monday it had been awarded a contract worth over $10 million to provide a network of satellite communications terminals for Brazil's armed forces, known as SISCOMIS.</p>
<p>Matra Marconi said it would supply shipborne communications for the Brazilian navy along with some land-based tactical mobile terminals for use by the navy, army and air force.</p>
<p>It will also provide a central hub station and network management facilities.</p>
<p>Matra Marconi will be prime contractor and will work closely with Brazil's Promon Eletronica.</p>
<p>The network will use X-band transponders on the latest generation BRASILSAT satellites currently in orbit, Matra Marconi said.</p>
<p>Matra Marconi is a joint venture between Lagardere of France and GEC of the UK.</p>
